# Webview Bundle · electron-forge

Run a electron-forge app with a local Webview Bundle.

## Prerequisites

Node.js 22.12 or later.

## Start

Install dependencies and run the app:

```sh
{{installCommand}}
{{devCommand}}
```

The `dev` script opens the desktop application. Use `{{buildCommand}}` to build it.

The app displays a counter. Edit `webview/public/` and run `{{devCommand}}` again to rebuild the builtin bundle. `wvb.config.ts` packs the local `webview` project; no remote server is required.

Before distributing your app, change the native app name and identifier in its platform configuration. See the [Webview Bundle documentation](https://wvb.dev/docs) for remote updates.

The `build:main` and `build:preload` scripts compile main and preload sources with esbuild. The main build keeps `@wvb/electron` external; Forge includes its runtime files when packaging. The `dev`, `build`, and `make` scripts run both builds before starting Forge. Edit `src/main.ts` and `src/preload.ts` to change native behavior.
